{"title":"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Alternative_thinking\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative thinking</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> logarithms of the divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bedd46306390e4c9b9293a00c7de6620b71b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ced7bf3e304ebb9fb9c073a8e5c5fde1740873a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$792$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/2387a93acc2a27138978fb166fa35ca20afb51b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 11\\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 12\\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 13\\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 14\\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Every factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bedd46306390e4c9b9293a00c7de6620b71b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> will be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f689771449c723b9c061c322eac816a5dc22a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^a \\times 5^b , a\\leq n , b\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />. Not all of these base ten logarithms will be rational, but we can add them together in a certain way to make it rational. Recall the logarithmic property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e403a4f6aba0b21b006739e89c2e49581ca7bc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(a \\times b) = \\log(a)+\\log(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />. For any factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095949f58b548c3e3a3af1aeaa455d2686f7077b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^a \\times 5^b$\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, there will be another factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae26e8d7813cd548f522a9c63f37212f93cab33b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-a} \\times 5^{n-b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" />. Note this is not true if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bedd46306390e4c9b9293a00c7de6620b71b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is a perfect square. When these are multiplied, they equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e07efca5e2789d730160e0b43fe500b93a7953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a+n-a} \\times 5^{b+n-b} = 10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"19\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c4046907467b32838252b04ed0461ba08d7906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log 10^n=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" /> so the number of factors divided by 2 times n equals the sum of all the factors, 792. \n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> choices for the exponent of 5 in each factor, and for each of those choices, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> factors (each corresponding to a different exponent of 2), yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57efb5c0b218135087ac110b8467426b528d7856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> total factors. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c0621e3055d14adb0fa4c05c6ebe14f97db1a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(n+1)^2}{2}*n = 792$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"39\" />. We then plug in answer choices and arrive at the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef74a6d9807de1430cd166c76eec1260199eadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56589b20a27d17fe83c721d0e2bd223f73e0d9e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10}d_1 + \\log_{10}d_2 + \\ldots + \\log_{10}d_k = 792\\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"17\" /> The property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370ca7cdf35237898cf202373aa503994dbb1579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(ab) = \\log(a)+\\log(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" /> now gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/80372cedd8b1188582f0569720bf36269e9b64a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10}(d_1 d_2\\cdot\\ldots d_k) = 792\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" /> The product of the divisors is (from elementary number theory) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59e548337b5c76ccfbfa44e45ebe67a97e782cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{d(n)/2}$\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05725a6508fe8df761c6e91d2735b697ebd87d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of divisors. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6d141d925d12ffe7fd49968e15f0d0f009de21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n = 2^n\\cdot 5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dca5b9f769b87cd1f72b60ad73b12df0825d5d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(n) = (n + 1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />. Substituting these values with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/6347f811b411663ade9d971010ffbb39f5f8a70d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> in our equation above, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4df64be582d8dab6867dfb86378b05220c06c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n + 1)^2 = 1584$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"19\" />, from whence we immediately obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8ddf002fb952ca8e675a6203b24d8d8bdc967e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\framebox[1.2\\width]{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"31\" height=\"28\" /> as the correct answer.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For every divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bedd46306390e4c9b9293a00c7de6620b71b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/032192e19811c0715ae14a9f386dcb23a452ddd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d \\le \\sqrt{10^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06b308fd136eec027f386b833d0509067184c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log d + \\log \\frac{10^n}{d} = \\log 10^n = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"228\" height=\"37\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb3d839d5ede2cff78681306acb636d94f5381f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor \\frac{(n+1)^2}{2} \\right \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"84\" height=\"43\" /> divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c8df5d77246a2c8b416a362b08671a0533c5f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n = 2^n \\times 5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" /> that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b750dae7b5a45431f78f4896114b09055747062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le \\sqrt{10^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" />. After casework on the parity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we find that the answer is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbf54cf19e1aa6172ac1b2cb7ff9f3de2a88d44f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times \\frac{(n+1)^2}{2} = 792 \\Longrightarrow n = 11\\ \\mathrm{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"276\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The sum is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c38f57f0aa17c542dcf7ebdff1c7c83adc74e38.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{p=0}^{n}\\sum_{q=0}^{n} \\log(2^p5^q) = \\sum_{p=0}^{n}\\sum_{q=0}^{n}(p\\log(2)+q\\log(5))\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"49\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cabf3a8d814d391dfcd62a4bac26b8ef3a1d699a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\sum_{p=0}^{n} ((n+1)p\\log(2) + \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\log(5))\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"49\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3d31bcd2c41b361df4a1c5ce95cbe62b881c123.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{n(n+1)^2}{2} \\log(2) + \\frac{n(n+1)^2}{2} \\log(5)\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/1495da22c9df4bd8efee515f7eb9c21deac3f879.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{n(n+1)^2}{2}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"39\" />\nTrying for answer choices we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093e72c1ebd91ade8c33ce3bcc3ccd3e640cad8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of divisors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bedd46306390e4c9b9293a00c7de6620b71b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> has. Then, we set up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/0049275faba66d1146c7cab42dc026f0b71cee89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> pairs of divisors such that each pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b77845dfa6d849654bd365564208ac2df3d206c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = 10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> -- ex. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93a2457cee7b130363579b8dbbcf9c9a6781a769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 10^n), (2, 5*10^{n-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"21\" />, etc. Then the sum of the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> logarithms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8ed7ab65743b2de574d1dcb16ea63c557a0e5a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{d}{2}} \\log_{10} a_j + \\log_{10} b_j = \\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{d}{2}} \\log_{10} a_j b_j = \\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{d}{2}} \\log_{10} 10^n = \\sum_{j=1}^{\\frac{d}{2}} n = \\frac{nd}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"523\" height=\"63\" />\nWe can use the property that only perfect squares have an odd number of factors, as for perfect square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, we have ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff947434e8d911cc2c48214043c07d950858857d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> that works. For even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfacc2a6cef04ec148c098d066422567a127cc2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{\\frac{n}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> can be multiplied by itself to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bedd46306390e4c9b9293a00c7de6620b71b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. But, in our summation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/0049275faba66d1146c7cab42dc026f0b71cee89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> does not exist for even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is then odd, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be even. And, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8a4dc574295060f1f0b23c92fe8bb87a168e911.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{nd}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"39\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ced7bf3e304ebb9fb9c073a8e5c5fde1740873a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$792$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, We want to find a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for our odd options <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d18fe37d0a4ef803d3c18da7382c157b40696f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nd$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31820e0ac338552f157d7b484d16eebcca4b903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1584$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093e72c1ebd91ade8c33ce3bcc3ccd3e640cad8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19a0f9e946dfa8ad9aaba3da35798cb0c590039b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> works, and integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can not be found for other odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. So, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acf9528c9a455960535d1f08f0e8f4ecf67c69ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\framebox[1.2\\width]{(A) 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"59\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_thinking\">Alternative thinking</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative thinking\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After arriving at the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90a1118afc011d353982ec53a3e182ce4e1baaea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1)^2 = 1584$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"19\" />, notice that all of the answer choices are in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c1d3de510a33234a7e5b97ecd3fa49df05ef48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8edc124c7f7a2d3729f66545564dea7041aee003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />. We notice that the ones digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92ef0e959dd40d5c084352e0efb757e605f33225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and it is dependent on the ones digit of the answer choices. Trying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8edc124c7f7a2d3729f66545564dea7041aee003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we see that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yields a ones digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B\">2008 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a hre